# Zonewiki's deployment settings. Copy to .env (cp .env.example .env) and edit;
# .env is gitignored. Every setting is optional except ZONE_DATA. Uncomment a
# line to use it. Details: docs/spec/deployment.md.
#
# The wiki's own settings (a password or users, the MCP token, hosts, locale,
# sharing mode …) are in the wiki's settings file, .zone/config, which Zonewiki
# reloads without a restart: ./run.sh config passwd, ./run.sh user add alice,
# or edit it. See docs/spec/users.md.

# The wiki folder, which must exist (default ~/zonewiki). run.sh expands a ~.
# Used without run.sh, give an absolute path.
ZONE_DATA=~/zonewiki

# A folder that holds files (Markdown notes you have) and isn't a wiki yet
# is made one only when asked: set this for the first start. An empty folder
# needs nothing. docs/spec/deployment.md, A new wiki.
# ZONE_INIT=1

# Timezone, so "today" is your day (default: the host's, via run.sh; else UTC).
# TZ=Europe/Berlin

# Network access: 1 listens on the LAN (e.g. for your phone), default localhost
# only. Then any IP address reaches it (http://192.168.1.20:5080); a name
# (nas.local) goes in hosts in the settings file (zonewiki config set hosts …).
# ZONE_ALLOW_REMOTE=1

# Semantic search with a local model, baked in at build (adds about 1 GB).
# ZONE_SEMANTIC_SEARCH=on

# A public wiki: view lets anyone read the wiki's shared pages without signing
# in, edit lets them edit and make pages too (as "anonymous"). Visitors see
# no tasks, notes or private pages, and upload nothing. Needs users in the
# settings file. Unset: everyone signs in. docs/spec/security.md, Public wikis.
# ZONE_PUBLIC=view

# Sign-up: 1 lets anyone (or anyone at signup-domains) ask for an account at
# /signup with their mail address. Needs users and base-url in the settings
# file, and a mail server below; signup-role and signup-approval there say
# what an account gets (default: viewer, no approval). docs/spec/users.md.
# ZONE_SIGNUP=1

# The mail server Zonewiki sends sign-up mail through. TLS: starttls (default,
# port 587; the server must offer it), tls (port 465), or none (a relay that
# takes mail unencrypted). The password goes only over TLS, or to localhost.
# ZONE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.org
# ZONE_SMTP_PORT=587
# ZONE_SMTP_USER=wiki@example.org
# ZONE_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# ZONE_SMTP_TLS=starttls
# ZONE_MAIL_FROM=wiki@example.org

# Not for compose: a Zonewiki that systemd starts on a socket it holds (zonewiki
# --addr fd:3) exits after this long without a request, and is started again
# by the next one. docs/spec/deployment.md, Started by systemd.
# ZONE_IDLE_EXIT=15m

# For docker compose without run.sh, which works them out itself (from
# ZONE_ALLOW_REMOTE and your user; set here, they win over that). Without
# run.sh, ZONE_DATA must be an absolute path, and compose.yaml (the prebuilt
# image) needs ZONE_UID/ZONE_GID, the wiki folder's owner.
# ZONE_BIND=0.0.0.0
# ZONE_UID=1000
# ZONE_GID=1000

# The port on the host, default 5080 (not 5000: macOS AirPlay Receiver and a
# Synology's DSM have that):
# ZONE_PORT=5081
